00:16:00.793 --> 00:16:02.194
I will try very hard

00:16:02.194 --> 00:16:03.529 align:start size:88% position:13%
to be more (indistinct)-
- Much obliged.

00:16:03.529 --> 00:16:04.496
than I was in the
first question.

00:16:04.496 --> 00:16:05.597
It's tricky stuff.

00:16:05.597 --> 00:16:06.832
I'll tell you why.

00:16:06.832 --> 00:16:08.901
And this is, I wrote a
whole book on miracles,

00:16:08.901 --> 00:16:13.639 align:start position:0%
and sometimes what makes a
miracle dramatic is the context.

00:16:13.639 --> 00:16:16.976
In other words, if God
is speaking to someone,

00:16:16.976 --> 00:16:18.711
it may make sense to that person

00:16:18.711 --> 00:16:21.513
because they bring a
whole bunch of context

00:16:21.513 --> 00:16:22.815
to that situation

00:16:22.815 --> 00:16:24.416 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it wouldn't mean
anything to anyone else.

00:16:24.416 --> 00:16:26.719
In my case, if you had
put a gun to my head

00:16:26.719 --> 00:16:30.089
at age 24 and said, who are you?

00:16:30.089 --> 00:16:32.791 align:start size:88% position:13%
In a dream or in a
fairytale, in your core,

00:16:32.791 --> 00:16:33.692
who are you?

00:16:35.928 --> 00:16:37.730
I don't think I could
have come up with it.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.366 align:start size:88% position:13%
But the most basic
elements, if they were,

00:16:40.366 --> 00:16:43.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
let's say three of who
I was at that point

00:16:43.435 --> 00:16:46.005 align:start size:84% position:16%
were the Greek
immigrant upbringing

00:16:46.005 --> 00:16:48.207
was at the center of my life.

00:16:48.207 --> 00:16:49.341
There's no question.

00:16:50.509 --> 00:16:55.347
And the second thing
was that for all of my

00:16:57.349 --> 00:17:01.086
teen years or childhood or
whatever, I was fishing.

00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:02.755
When I wasn't watching TV,

00:17:02.755 --> 00:17:04.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
when I wasn't watching
"Sanford and Son"

00:17:04.356 --> 00:17:06.992
and "The Dean Martin
Roast," I was fishing.

00:17:06.992 --> 00:17:08.761
And that's just what I did.

00:17:08.761 --> 00:17:10.229
So I never got in trouble.

00:17:10.229 --> 00:17:12.598
I studied, I watched TV,
and I did a lot of fishing,

00:17:12.598 --> 00:17:13.966
so that was a big part of me.

00:17:13.966 --> 00:17:18.837 align:start size:97% position:3%
But also a weird connection
is that my father,

00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:21.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
whenever he saw, 'cause
all Greeks are evangelists

00:17:21.774 --> 00:17:23.275
for being Greek.

00:17:23.275 --> 00:17:25.177 align:start size:84% position:16%
Their number one
hobby is being Greek.

00:17:25.177 --> 00:17:27.446 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so my father,
anytime he saw a fish,

00:17:27.446 --> 00:17:29.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
a chrome fish on the back
of a car in the '70s,

00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:32.418
he would say, you see that fish?

00:17:32.418 --> 00:17:34.453
That comes from the Greek word,

00:17:34.453 --> 00:17:35.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
because the early
Christians couldn't use

00:17:35.888 --> 00:17:36.822
the sign of the cross,

00:17:36.822 --> 00:17:38.757
they used the symbol of the fish

00:17:38.757 --> 00:17:40.159
because the Greek word for fish,

00:17:40.159 --> 00:17:42.194
the ancient word is ichthys,

00:17:42.194 --> 00:17:43.529
it's where we get ichthyologist.

00:17:43.529 --> 00:17:47.566 align:start size:88% position:13%
And ichthys, the
words, it's an acronym,

00:17:47.566 --> 00:17:50.035
(speaking in foreign language)

00:17:50.035 --> 00:17:52.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
It spells Jesus Christ,
the son of God our savior.

00:17:52.971 --> 00:17:55.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so they use the
secret symbol of the fish

00:17:55.374 --> 00:17:57.276
and my father says to me
in Danbury, Connecticut,

00:17:57.276 --> 00:17:58.544
on the highway,

00:17:58.544 --> 00:18:00.012
"You see that fish,
it's a Greek word."

00:18:00.012 --> 00:18:01.413 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he gets all excited about
the fact that it's Greek.

00:18:01.413 --> 00:18:02.915
Now, I'm being a little unfair.

00:18:02.915 --> 00:18:05.751
I think he was aware of
the Christian element,

00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:09.588
but he was very excited that
the fish, it's a Greek word.

00:18:09.588 --> 00:18:12.291 align:start size:84% position:16%
So in any event, the
third part of me,

00:18:12.291 --> 00:18:13.492
if you're gonna say
there's fishing,

00:18:13.492 --> 00:18:15.160 align:start size:88% position:13%
there's the Greek thing,
the third part of me

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:16.562
was what I call the
life of the mind.

00:18:16.562 --> 00:18:18.430
From age 16 to 24,

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.132 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm trying to figure
out the meaning of life.

00:18:20.132 --> 00:18:23.268
I'm trying to figure out,
who am I, why am I here?

00:18:23.268 --> 00:18:25.003 align:start size:84% position:16%
And whenever I was
reading the literature

00:18:25.003 --> 00:18:26.672
that I was reading in college,

00:18:26.672 --> 00:18:28.874
I wasn't reading it the
way most people read it.

00:18:28.874 --> 00:18:33.645
I was trying to figure out
what is the clue to humanity?

00:18:33.645 --> 00:18:34.880
Who are we?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.416
And it's good art,
that's what it does.

00:18:37.416 --> 00:18:39.852 align:start size:97% position:3%
It helps you understand what
does it mean to be human

00:18:39.852 --> 00:18:41.086
and so on and so forth.

00:18:41.086 --> 00:18:43.222
So I was trying to
puzzle this out,

00:18:43.222 --> 00:18:45.057 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I remember
that at some point,

00:18:45.057 --> 00:18:48.994
just after graduating and
getting the woke memo,

00:18:48.994 --> 00:18:51.396
that Christianity
is too parochial,

00:18:51.396 --> 00:18:54.900
the Bible, it's just a
bunch of right bigots.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.136
But if there's any religion,

00:18:57.136 --> 00:18:59.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
it probably combines
all religions,

00:18:59.738 --> 00:19:02.608
and it's probably more
like a new age life force

00:19:02.608 --> 00:19:03.842
or something like that.

00:19:03.842 --> 00:19:05.344
And I came up with
this idea in my own,

00:19:05.344 --> 00:19:08.113
that you know what, it's
sort of like Freud's idea

00:19:08.113 --> 00:19:09.348
of the soul.

00:19:09.348 --> 00:19:12.951 align:start size:81% position:19%
Where you have
the conscious mind

00:19:12.951 --> 00:19:16.054 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then you have
the unconscious below
the conscious mind.

00:19:16.054 --> 00:19:18.557 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I kind of brought
in a little Jung,

00:19:18.557 --> 00:19:20.325
this is supposed to
sound pretentious.

00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:21.860
I was an undergraduate.

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:26.298 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I have this idea, that
maybe the goal of life is that

00:19:26.298 --> 00:19:29.468 align:start size:84% position:16%
the ice on the lake
is the conscious mind.

00:19:29.468 --> 00:19:32.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that the water beneath
it is the unconscious

00:19:32.571 --> 00:19:35.107
or what Yong calls the
collective unconscious,

00:19:35.107 --> 00:19:38.143
which is this God force
or something like that.

00:19:38.143 --> 00:19:39.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought maybe
that's what all religions

00:19:39.478 --> 00:19:40.712
are getting at.

00:19:40.712 --> 00:19:43.382
So the goal of life is
to drill through the ice

00:19:43.382 --> 00:19:46.485 align:start size:97% position:3%
so that you have an an
emotionally healthy connection

00:19:46.485 --> 00:19:49.054 align:start size:97% position:3%
between the conscious mind and
the collective unconscious,

00:19:49.054 --> 00:19:51.290
or God or whatever it is.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.992
Now, what does that
mean practically?

00:19:53.992 --> 00:19:55.961
Bupkis, nothing, of course.

00:19:55.961 --> 00:19:58.297
It just means like, yeah, I
figured that out, I got it.

00:19:58.297 --> 00:19:59.865
All religions say the same thing

00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:01.300
and I'm gonna move
on with my life.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.802 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that's really where
I was coming from,

00:20:03.802 --> 00:20:05.737
which of course led
me to be really lost.

00:20:05.737 --> 00:20:06.838
How do I live?

00:20:06.838 --> 00:20:08.040
What is right, what is wrong?

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.141
I had no idea.

00:20:09.141 --> 00:20:10.642
So I meet this guy.

00:20:10.642 --> 00:20:13.212
He talks to me about my
faith and faith whatever,

00:20:13.212 --> 00:20:14.846
we talked for about a year.

00:20:14.846 --> 00:20:17.115
And at the end of the
year, I had a dream.

00:20:17.115 --> 00:20:18.483
My uncle had just passed away

00:20:18.483 --> 00:20:21.420
so I was a little bit
emotionally vulnerable

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:26.124
and beginning to wonder, is
there something out there?

00:20:26.124 --> 00:20:29.261 align:start size:97% position:3%
And if there is, I feel
like I'm hermetically sealed

00:20:29.261 --> 00:20:31.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a room with no
windows and no doors.

00:20:31.129 --> 00:20:32.431
And if there's a God out there,

00:20:32.431 --> 00:20:34.333
he's gonna have to punch a hole

00:20:34.333 --> 00:20:36.602
through the wall
and say, I'm here.

00:20:36.602 --> 00:20:38.470
Because in the material world,

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:42.307 align:start size:88% position:13%
I have no way of
logically getting there.

00:20:42.307 --> 00:20:45.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
So in this dream, I'm
standing on a frozen lake

00:20:45.477 --> 00:20:46.812 align:start size:88% position:13%
in Danbury,
Connecticut, Candlewood,

00:20:46.812 --> 00:20:48.914
where I fish many times.

00:20:48.914 --> 00:20:52.150
And I looked down
and in the hole,

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.119
and this never happens if
you're an ice fishermen,

00:20:54.119 --> 00:20:57.522
there's a fish sticking
its snout out of a hole.

00:20:57.522 --> 00:21:01.159
And I reached down and I
pick it up by the gills,

00:21:01.159 --> 00:21:02.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it's like a
pickerel or a pike.

00:21:02.661 --> 00:21:04.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's one of those bronze,
golden-colored fish.

00:21:04.997 --> 00:21:07.799
And I pick it up and
it's one of these,

00:21:07.799 --> 00:21:09.868
in a dream like this, I'd
never had a dream like this

00:21:09.868 --> 00:21:12.204
ever in my life, nor since.

00:21:12.204 --> 00:21:16.508 align:start size:81% position:19%
It was like the
perfect winter day

00:21:16.508 --> 00:21:19.911 align:start size:84% position:16%
where the snow and the
ice are super white

00:21:19.911 --> 00:21:23.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the sky is super blue,
and it's just glorious.

00:21:23.515 --> 00:21:26.718
And I hold up this golden
fish into the sunlight.

00:21:26.718 --> 00:21:31.723
And in the dream, suddenly I
know, this is the golden fish.

00:21:34.126 --> 00:21:35.627
This is ichthys.

00:21:35.627 --> 00:21:39.097
This is all, God's one up
to me with my symbol system

00:21:39.097 --> 00:21:43.068 align:start position:0%
and these two paragraphs dropped
into my head in the dream,

00:21:43.068 --> 00:21:47.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
that you wanted to touch
inert water, this God force,

00:21:47.773 --> 00:21:49.474 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I had something
else for you,

00:21:49.474 --> 00:21:52.444
my son, your savior,
Jesus Christ, ichthys.

00:21:52.444 --> 00:21:54.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
And this all came
together in the dream.

00:21:54.413 --> 00:21:55.947
And the weird thing
is in the dream,

00:21:55.947 --> 00:21:58.083 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm holding this fish up,
and I realized in the dream,

00:21:58.083 --> 00:22:00.852
it looks golden as though
it's actually made of gold,

00:22:00.852 --> 00:22:02.054 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then I realized
in the dream,

00:22:02.054 --> 00:22:04.690
no, it is made of gold.

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:07.492 align:start size:88% position:13%
It is a golden fish that
is nonetheless alive,

00:22:07.492 --> 00:22:09.528
like out of a fairytale.

00:22:09.528 --> 00:22:13.432 align:start position:0%
And at that moment in the dream,
my mind was totally blown.

00:22:13.432 --> 00:22:16.635
I knew that God had my number,

00:22:16.635 --> 00:22:19.604
that he spoke to me in a
way that made sense to me,

00:22:19.604 --> 00:22:22.607
that the thing that I
had convinced myself

00:22:22.607 --> 00:22:25.644 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
was impossible for
intelligent people to know,

00:22:25.644 --> 00:22:28.347 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
you could maybe
hope that it's true.

00:22:28.347 --> 00:22:31.750 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
That suddenly I knew
it, I was stuck with it.

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:33.452 line:0%
I would have to deal with
it for the rest of my life

00:22:33.452 --> 00:22:34.720
but I couldn't go back,

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:37.656
I couldn't pretend that
God hadn't spoken to me

00:22:37.656 --> 00:22:38.924
in this miraculous way,

00:22:38.924 --> 00:22:41.093
which revealed that
he knew more about me

00:22:41.093 --> 00:22:42.527
than I knew about myself.

00:22:42.527 --> 00:22:45.097 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now that is the short
version of it, I apologize.

00:22:45.097 --> 00:22:46.365
- No, no, no.

00:22:46.365 --> 00:22:47.265
Well, there's a lot
there, so let's go.

00:22:47.265 --> 00:22:49.201
So when you have this,

00:22:49.201 --> 00:22:51.036 align:start size:84% position:16%
now you have this
revelation, let's say.

00:22:51.036 --> 00:22:52.371
- Yeah.

00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:54.606
- You're obviously
an intellectual guy.

00:22:54.606 --> 00:22:57.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
That seems to be where
much of the thrust

00:22:57.075 --> 00:22:59.211
of your passion is.

00:22:59.211 --> 00:23:00.946
Did you freak out after that,

00:23:00.946 --> 00:23:02.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
like this was
gonna somehow erode

00:23:02.781 --> 00:23:04.616
the intellectual
side of yourself?

00:23:04.616 --> 00:23:05.851
- No.

00:23:05.851 --> 00:23:07.219
- Or turn you in the
eyes of your friends,

00:23:07.219 --> 00:23:08.120
something like that?

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:09.321
- Well, yes.

00:23:09.321 --> 00:23:11.323 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, for sure, I knew
that would happen.

00:23:11.323 --> 00:23:12.791
But this is where, I mean, look,

00:23:12.791 --> 00:23:16.528 align:start size:97% position:3%
let's say you're in the
woods and you meet Bigfoot,

00:23:16.528 --> 00:23:21.433 align:start position:0%
and you know you're not an
idiot, you're not on mushrooms,

00:23:21.433 --> 00:23:22.868
it actually happened.

00:23:24.302 --> 00:23:27.539
There are people that are
never gonna believe you,

00:23:27.539 --> 00:23:28.974
but you're stuck.

00:23:28.974 --> 00:23:32.043 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can't convince yourself
that it didn't happen.

00:23:33.211 --> 00:23:36.014
It's one of those things
where, when I woke up,

00:23:36.014 --> 00:23:38.617
I knew this was real,
I knew this was true,

00:23:38.617 --> 00:23:41.553
I knew the Bible is the word
of God, I know Jesus is way,

00:23:41.553 --> 00:23:44.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I knew all my friends
would think I'm nuts

00:23:44.689 --> 00:23:46.892
or pat me on the head
and go like, whatever.

00:23:48.026 --> 00:23:51.630
But the point is I
didn't have a choice.

00:23:51.630 --> 00:23:55.233 align:start size:97% position:3%
I couldn't say, you know what,
I'm just gonna ignore this.

00:23:55.233 --> 00:23:57.869
It was too powerful to ignore.

00:23:57.869 --> 00:23:59.805
It wasn't something
I could walk from.

00:23:59.805 --> 00:24:04.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was God crafting a
message literally for me,

00:24:06.144 --> 00:24:07.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a way, calculated by
the author of the universe

00:24:07.546 --> 00:24:08.713
to blow my mind.

00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:10.215
My mind was blown.

00:24:10.215 --> 00:24:13.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
But the funny thing
is, Dave, that I knew,

00:24:13.118 --> 00:24:15.687
I remember going to work the
next day to tell my friend,

00:24:15.687 --> 00:24:16.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
this Christian who
had been talking to me

00:24:16.888 --> 00:24:18.890
and I tell him a little
bit about the dream,

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:20.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
he goes, "What do
you think it means?"

00:24:20.592 --> 00:24:23.495
And I said, "I've
accepted Jesus."

00:24:23.495 --> 00:24:26.598
Now, I would've never,
I would have cringed

00:24:26.598 --> 00:24:30.302 align:start size:84% position:16%
to speak those words
anytime before.

00:24:30.302 --> 00:24:33.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I said it to
him like, it's done.

00:24:33.738 --> 00:24:37.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whatever that means,
that's what happened now.

00:24:37.275 --> 00:24:40.445
I didn't start voting for
Republicans the next day.

00:24:40.445 --> 00:24:42.280
It took a time for me to begin

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:43.715
to process this,

00:24:43.715 --> 00:24:48.620 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I knew that I would
challenge most of my friends,

00:24:50.422 --> 00:24:51.690
would be tough for them.

00:24:51.690 --> 00:24:55.293
And the ones who were
willing to hear me out

00:24:55.293 --> 00:24:57.429
and to continue to be my friend,

00:24:59.030 --> 00:25:00.966 align:start position:0%
that's kind of where you realize
who your real friends are,

00:25:00.966 --> 00:25:05.971
in a sense, because they
accorded me enough dignity

00:25:07.105 --> 00:25:10.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
to try to understand
what I was telling them.

00:25:10.175 --> 00:25:12.077
And the funny thing too, is that

00:25:12.077 --> 00:25:17.082
I never was a like in
your face about it,

00:25:17.949 --> 00:25:21.586
but they acted as though I was.

00:25:21.586 --> 00:25:23.121 align:start size:88% position:13%
I remember having
lunch here in Manhattan

00:25:23.121 --> 00:25:27.225
with a sophisticated
friend, and saying,

00:25:27.225 --> 00:25:31.363 align:start size:97% position:3%
just kind of telling him this
in a very, very gingerly,

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:32.497
and him sort of exploding, like,

00:25:32.497 --> 00:25:33.431
"What are you saying?

00:25:33.431 --> 00:25:34.399
Everybody's going to hell."

00:25:34.399 --> 00:25:37.402
He just is all over me.

00:25:37.402 --> 00:25:39.337 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I just thought,
this is what,

00:25:39.337 --> 00:25:41.606 align:start size:84% position:16%
this is gonna be
the rest of my life.

00:25:41.606 --> 00:25:44.943
But it's not that different
from coming out for Trump.

00:25:44.943 --> 00:25:46.478
Some people are gonna hate you,

00:25:46.478 --> 00:25:48.346
some people are gonna
think you're evil.

00:25:48.346 --> 00:25:49.681
Some people are gonna love you.

00:25:49.681 --> 00:25:50.916
The fact of the matter

00:25:50.916 --> 00:25:53.451
is that at some point
you have no choice.

00:25:53.451 --> 00:25:57.989 align:start position:0%
When that happened in the
summer of 1988, I had no choice.

00:25:57.989 --> 00:26:02.427
I had to do my best to
represent it as I could.

00:26:02.427 --> 00:26:05.764
And I've many ways failed
and in some ways succeeded,

00:26:05.764 --> 00:26:08.867
but there's just no
going back from that.

00:26:08.867 --> 00:26:10.702
I wanted a miracle,
I got a miracle.

00:26:10.702 --> 00:26:12.137
And I've had many miracles
that have happened to me

00:26:12.137 --> 00:26:14.272
actually since then,

00:26:14.272 --> 00:26:17.809
which I give the,

00:26:17.809 --> 00:26:19.945
they rise to the bar of
calling them miracles.

00:26:19.945 --> 00:26:23.081 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm not talking about
blessings, oh that was nice.

00:26:23.081 --> 00:26:25.517 align:start size:81% position:19%
That is real, I've
experienced it,

00:26:25.517 --> 00:26:27.385
not as much as I would like.

00:26:27.385 --> 00:26:29.888
But at this point
we could debate

00:26:29.888 --> 00:26:31.990
all kinds of stuff forever,

00:26:31.990 --> 00:26:34.693 align:start size:97% position:3%
but if somebody asks me, are
you sure about the Jesus,

00:26:34.693 --> 00:26:35.527
are you sure have it?

00:26:35.527 --> 00:26:36.895
There was no question.

00:26:36.895 --> 00:26:38.163
You can torture me,

00:26:38.163 --> 00:26:40.098
there's nothing I can
do to convince myself

00:26:40.098 --> 00:26:42.901
that I might've missed
something at this point.

00:26:42.901 --> 00:26:44.402
- So speaking of miss something,

00:26:44.402 --> 00:26:47.372 align:start size:84% position:16%
then do you think
that most academics,

00:26:47.372 --> 00:26:50.308
like your friend that you
sat with who brought up

00:26:50.308 --> 00:26:52.277 align:start size:84% position:16%
burning in hell
and the rest of it,

00:26:52.277 --> 00:26:55.347
do you think that that
is the fundamental flaw

00:26:55.347 --> 00:26:58.316
of most academics
that then is partly

00:26:58.316 --> 00:27:00.518 align:start size:97% position:3%
why we're watching
academia crumble right now,

00:27:00.518 --> 00:27:02.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they've
disconnected these things

00:27:02.253 --> 00:27:04.122
or they've mocked believers

00:27:04.122 --> 00:27:06.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the point that they've
been left with this?

00:27:06.358 --> 00:27:07.459
I'll just mention
one other thing,

00:27:07.459 --> 00:27:09.294
which is I had John Kasich,

00:27:09.294 --> 00:27:13.598 align:start size:97% position:3%
the former governor of Ohio
on, he's the governor of Ohio.

00:27:13.598 --> 00:27:16.801 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he said something
interesting to me about this.

00:27:16.801 --> 00:27:19.437
He said, "You know, a lot of
people can do it without God.

00:27:19.437 --> 00:27:20.972
I'm just not one
of those people."

00:27:20.972 --> 00:27:23.475 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I brought it up in
many interviews since then.

00:27:23.475 --> 00:27:26.111 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because it's not
the most enlightened
thing I've ever heard,

00:27:26.111 --> 00:27:28.713
it's actually very
humbling and decent,

00:27:28.713 --> 00:27:31.282 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I found it to be
really refreshingly honest.

00:27:31.282 --> 00:27:33.084
Do you sense there's
some connection there

00:27:33.084 --> 00:27:35.120
between the way the
intellectual elite

00:27:35.120 --> 00:27:36.688
seem to be crumbling right now?

00:27:36.688 --> 00:27:40.425
- There's zero question
that the answer is yes.

00:27:40.425 --> 00:27:41.459
There's no question.

00:27:41.459 --> 00:27:42.494
Look, it's all related.

00:27:42.494 --> 00:27:44.129
It's not just about God.

00:27:44.129 --> 00:27:46.197
I'll give an example,
at a place like Yale,

00:27:46.197 --> 00:27:50.669 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you are somebody like
Miroslav Volf, okay.

00:27:50.669 --> 00:27:53.571
He's a serious Christian,
but he's pretty left wing.

00:27:54.506 --> 00:27:56.474
So they'll give him a pass.

00:27:58.543 --> 00:28:00.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
It really is, but
it's very interesting,

00:28:00.712 --> 00:28:03.648 align:start size:97% position:3%
what are the different
shibboleths that people have?

00:28:03.648 --> 00:28:05.483 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like, you can
say anything you want,

00:28:05.483 --> 00:28:08.653
but if you don't believe
a woman should be able

00:28:08.653 --> 00:28:13.658
to kill what's in her womb,
you're a pig and a bigot.

00:28:14.859 --> 00:28:17.862
And it's interesting
how that works out.

00:28:17.862 --> 00:28:20.865
And I think that academia,

00:28:22.033 --> 00:28:23.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's funny 'cause I've
written about this.

00:28:23.501 --> 00:28:26.171
You can trace this way
back to the '20s, really,

00:28:26.171 --> 00:28:27.605
that it's like we
were saying earlier

00:28:27.605 --> 00:28:29.441 align:start size:84% position:16%
that there's this
trickle down effect.

00:28:29.441 --> 00:28:33.111
These ideas were
seeded S-E-E-D-E-D,

00:28:33.111 --> 00:28:37.916 align:start size:84% position:16%
seeded into the
culture in many ways.

00:28:39.117 --> 00:28:42.387
From Darwin to Nicha
to Freud, whatever.

00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:45.757 align:start size:97% position:3%
But they came into the
culture big time in the '20s.

00:28:45.757 --> 00:28:48.193
Margaret Mead was popular,

00:28:48.193 --> 00:28:52.497 align:start size:84% position:16%
having sex with anyone
you like in Samoa.

00:28:52.497 --> 00:28:57.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
This kind of vague
Freudian scientific reason

00:28:57.368 --> 00:29:01.372
for doing as we liked
became popularized.

00:29:01.372 --> 00:29:04.709
But it didn't trickle
down to middle America

00:29:04.709 --> 00:29:07.479
until you get to the '60s.

00:29:07.479 --> 00:29:09.914 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it still didn't trickle
down to the effected,

00:29:09.914 --> 00:29:11.983
continues to trickle down,

00:29:11.983 --> 00:29:16.755 align:start size:84% position:16%
so that now we have
arsonists and looters,

00:29:16.755 --> 00:29:20.792 align:start size:88% position:13%
and potential murderers
who are pretending

00:29:20.792 --> 00:29:22.594 align:start size:84% position:16%
to care about the
death of a black man

00:29:22.594 --> 00:29:25.296 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the way that Martin
Luther King Jr.,

00:29:25.296 --> 00:29:28.633 align:start size:97% position:3%
Rosa Parks, Jackie
Robinson would spit on them

00:29:28.633 --> 00:29:31.469 align:start size:84% position:16%
for the desecration
of the memory

00:29:31.469 --> 00:29:34.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
of those who have suffered
under real racism.

00:29:35.540 --> 00:29:39.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
The dissent from true American
self-government and Liberty

00:29:39.911 --> 00:29:43.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
into cultural Marxism
doesn't happen overnight,

00:29:43.248 --> 00:29:45.216
but that's effectively
what we're looking at.

00:29:45.216 --> 00:29:47.585
And Christianity to me,

00:29:47.585 --> 00:29:50.755
in many ways has been
at the core of this.

00:29:50.755 --> 00:29:54.192
There's just no question that
when you talk about the West,

00:29:54.192 --> 00:29:56.594
and it's part of the reason
for the decline of Europe,

00:29:56.594 --> 00:29:58.863
when you jettison
the Christianity,

00:29:58.863 --> 00:30:00.999
