00:31:19.210 --> 00:31:20.478
I've written a lot of humor

00:31:20.478 --> 00:31:22.914
and when I do public
speaking and stuff,

00:31:22.914 --> 00:31:24.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's just a lot of
comedy and goofing around

00:31:24.716 --> 00:31:26.618
on my radio program.

00:31:26.618 --> 00:31:28.953
Some people think
of me as as funny.

00:31:28.953 --> 00:31:31.322
So I had this idea

00:31:31.322 --> 00:31:32.657
when Trump was elected-
- That's a good title

00:31:32.657 --> 00:31:34.726
for a book, that's a
good title for a book.

00:31:34.726 --> 00:31:36.561
Some people think
of me as funny.

00:31:36.561 --> 00:31:37.662
(both laugh)

00:31:37.662 --> 00:31:38.496
- I'm not gonna use it.

00:31:38.496 --> 00:31:39.364
I give that to you.

00:31:39.364 --> 00:31:40.932
- No, no, thank you.

00:31:40.932 --> 00:31:44.435 align:start size:97% position:3%
- But the thing is that I
like humor, I like sad tale.

00:31:44.435 --> 00:31:46.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've even published
humor in "The New Yorker"

00:31:46.971 --> 00:31:48.840
and in "The Atlantic" and stuff.

00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:51.009
I've loved that kind of thing.

00:31:51.009 --> 00:31:55.113 align:start size:97% position:3%
And when Trump was
elected, I said to the guy,

00:31:55.113 --> 00:31:58.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
my dear friend, Tim
Raglin who lives in Kansas

00:31:58.549 --> 00:32:00.485
and he and I have done a
number of books together.

00:32:00.485 --> 00:32:01.986
He's a genius illustrator.

00:32:01.986 --> 00:32:04.889 align:start size:97% position:3%
This stuff we've done together
is just, it's stunning.

00:32:04.889 --> 00:32:06.090
But I said to him, Tim you know,

00:32:06.090 --> 00:32:07.792
you're the one that convinced me

00:32:07.792 --> 00:32:09.294
to look differently at Trump,

00:32:09.294 --> 00:32:11.296
when I was still like, I
don't know about that guy.

00:32:11.296 --> 00:32:13.498
I'm a New Yorker and
he's sort of vulgar,

00:32:13.498 --> 00:32:16.401
and I'm a Christian and
he's not my first pick.

00:32:16.401 --> 00:32:19.871
And he had me look at him
differently and I said,

00:32:19.871 --> 00:32:22.874
Trump is like, he's
like a folk hero.

00:32:22.874 --> 00:32:24.208
He's like out of
one of these books

00:32:24.208 --> 00:32:25.510
that I've written
with Tim Raglin,

00:32:25.510 --> 00:32:27.545
he's larger than life
like a cartoon figure.

00:32:27.545 --> 00:32:28.780
And I said to Tim,

00:32:28.780 --> 00:32:32.083 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Tim, we need to do
like a children's book

00:32:32.083 --> 00:32:34.619
about a character,
a Trump character,

00:32:34.619 --> 00:32:37.922
