politically correct.

00:37:00.751 --> 00:37:02.386
There's a lot of stuff about him

00:37:02.386 --> 00:37:06.557
that wouldn't work among your
friends, but you love him.

00:37:06.557 --> 00:37:08.226
And you know he's a good man,

00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:09.961 align:start size:81% position:19%
and you know he
loves his country,

00:37:09.961 --> 00:37:12.630
and he would fight and
die for his country.

00:37:12.630 --> 00:37:17.134
And if you're in trouble, you
want him around, he's good.

00:37:18.069 --> 00:37:19.303
But he's rough around the edges

00:37:19.303 --> 00:37:20.905
and he's got a lot of
things and you say,

00:37:20.905 --> 00:37:22.073
please, don't say that.

00:37:22.073 --> 00:37:23.407 align:start size:84% position:16%
Whatever you do,
please don't say that

00:37:23.407 --> 00:37:24.642
when my friends are over there.

00:37:24.642 --> 00:37:26.410
They're not gonna
understand that.

00:37:26.410 --> 00:37:29.080
And I began to see
that side of him

00:37:29.080 --> 00:37:30.815
and then I also realized
that because I grew up

00:37:30.815 --> 00:37:32.650
in a working class environment,

00:37:34.619 --> 00:37:36.721
he speaks to the working class.

00:37:36.721 --> 00:37:38.589
Martin Luther, about
whom I've also written,

00:37:38.589 --> 00:37:40.524
had this similar ability.

00:37:40.524 --> 00:37:42.793
Even though Trump
went to Wharton

00:37:42.793 --> 00:37:46.130
and is obviously an
instinctive genius.

00:37:46.130 --> 00:37:47.598
There's no question about it,

00:37:47.598 --> 00:37:49.500 align:start size:97% position:3%
but he has an ability to
connect with work and class,

00:37:49.500 --> 00:37:52.370
and a big part of that
is humor and hyperbole.

00:37:52.370 --> 00:37:56.207
And I began to hear
him differently, and
I began to think,

00:37:56.207 --> 00:37:59.844 align:start size:97% position:3%
wow, the cultural elites,
they don't get that language.

00:37:59.844 --> 00:38:01.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like you may as well
be speaking Japanese.

00:38:01.979 --> 00:38:03.314
They don't get it.

00:38:03.314 --> 00:38:05.816 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so, I began to
appreciate him more and more.

00:38:05.816 --> 00:38:10.821 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I have to say that if
anything ever revealed to me

00:38:12.123 --> 00:38:14.125 align:start size:97% position:3%
how pathetic the Republican
Party had become,

00:38:14.125 --> 00:38:17.128
when they turned against
him the way that he did,

00:38:17.128 --> 00:38:21.499
I mean, his ability to
see the problem in China,

00:38:21.499 --> 00:38:24.735
for example, we'll just
talk about a minor thing.

00:38:24.735 --> 00:38:26.170
Really minor, right?

00:38:26.170 --> 00:38:29.073 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, right.
- 1.3 billion people,

00:38:31.642 --> 00:38:34.945 align:start size:88% position:13%
the level of seriousness
that our leaders

00:38:34.945 --> 00:38:38.616
ought to have accorded China
over the last three decades

00:38:38.616 --> 00:38:42.653
is so huge and they
basically ignored it

00:38:42.653 --> 00:38:44.522
while it grew into a monster.

00:38:44.522 --> 00:38:46.724
Trump, if he did nothing else,

00:38:46.724 --> 00:38:48.526 align:start size:84% position:16%
diagnose the problem
30 years ago,

00:38:48.526 --> 00:38:50.061 align:start size:84% position:16%
has been talking
about it for 30 years

00:38:50.061 --> 00:38:54.098 align:start size:97% position:3%
and is now rather effectively
doing a number of things

00:38:54.098 --> 00:38:55.666
to deal with this problem.

00:38:55.666 --> 00:38:57.234
How much money is he making?

00:38:57.234 --> 00:39:00.538
A lot less than Hunter
Biden is making on China?

00:39:00.538 --> 00:39:01.972 align:start size:88% position:13%
I don't see him getting
anything out of it,

00:39:01.972 --> 00:39:04.608
except he feels it's the
right thing for America.

00:39:04.608 --> 00:39:07.078 align:start size:84% position:16%
So it's things like
that, that's just one.

00:39:07.078 --> 00:39:10.448
But he has been very
staunchly pro-life

00:39:10.448 --> 00:39:11.916
and staunchly religious liberty

00:39:11.916 --> 00:39:14.552 align:start size:97% position:3%
and these are the things that
have concerned me deeply.

00:39:14.552 --> 00:39:16.921 align:start size:88% position:13%
His willingness to
stand up for Kavanaugh.

00:39:16.921 --> 00:39:21.892
I would bet that a
lot of Republicans,

00:39:21.892 --> 00:39:24.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
people that I thought were
good guys 10 years ago,

00:39:24.362 --> 00:39:25.730
they would've folded at the end.

00:39:25.730 --> 00:39:29.467 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so, there's a
lot to recommend him

00:39:29.467 --> 00:39:31.202
and you're not supposed
to vote for somebody

00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:33.904
because you think they
share your theology.

00:39:35.373 --> 00:39:38.442
I don't really think that's
why you elect the president.

00:39:38.442 --> 00:39:41.946
It would be nice if he did,
