They all believed it,
there was no argument,

00:50:25.856 --> 00:50:27.424 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we're not
teaching it in school.

00:50:27.424 --> 00:50:29.860 align:start size:88% position:13%
So you think, so
freedom requires virtue,

00:50:29.860 --> 00:50:31.828 align:start size:84% position:16%
then the founders also
believe that virtue

00:50:31.828 --> 00:50:33.630
in turn required faith.

00:50:33.630 --> 00:50:36.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, they didn't
stipulate Christian faith,

00:50:36.233 --> 00:50:39.636
nor did they dare say
faith can be enforced,

00:50:39.636 --> 00:50:41.171
because they didn't
believe in that,

00:50:41.171 --> 00:50:45.942 align:start size:97% position:3%
but had seen that virtue needs
to be held up by something.

00:50:47.377 --> 00:50:49.212 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why do I do the right thing
when no one is looking?

00:50:49.212 --> 00:50:51.915
Why do I not loot when
I might not get caught?

00:50:51.915 --> 00:50:53.984
Well, because I answer
to a higher authority.

00:50:53.984 --> 00:50:55.285
They all observed this.

00:50:55.285 --> 00:50:56.953
Franklin observed
this most directly

00:50:56.953 --> 00:50:59.056 align:start size:84% position:16%
in all the preaching
of his friend,

00:50:59.056 --> 00:51:01.324
George Whitefield,
this evangelists.

00:51:01.324 --> 00:51:04.528
When revival broke
out, crime went down,

00:51:04.528 --> 00:51:07.497
domestic abuse went down,
self-government went up.

00:51:07.497 --> 00:51:10.000
They saw this happening up
and down the 13 colonies,

00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:12.702
and they saw that
faith was central.

00:51:12.702 --> 00:51:15.806
But then the third part,
freedom requires virtue,

00:51:15.806 --> 00:51:18.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
virtue requires faith, faith
in turn requires freedom.

00:51:18.975 --> 00:51:21.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
In other words, faith
cannot be forced,

00:51:21.745 --> 00:51:24.481
it cannot be enforced,
it can be encouraged,

00:51:26.983 --> 00:51:28.552
we can celebrate faith,

00:51:28.552 --> 00:51:31.088
but there's nothing
the government can do

00:51:31.088 --> 00:51:33.990
to force you or me
to believe something

00:51:33.990 --> 00:51:37.527 align:start size:97% position:3%
about these transcendent
things or to act virtuously.

00:51:37.527 --> 00:51:40.263 align:start size:97% position:3%
Maybe can force us to act
virtuously at the end of a gun

00:51:40.263 --> 00:51:41.565
but then it's no longer virtue,

00:51:41.565 --> 00:51:42.732
so in fact, they can't do that.

00:51:42.732 --> 00:51:45.068
So the founders got this,

00:51:45.068 --> 00:51:47.537 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they really
understood something

00:51:47.537 --> 00:51:49.673
that had never been
understood before.

00:51:49.673 --> 00:51:54.644
And so, if you think about it,
there's just no escaping it.

00:51:54.644 --> 00:51:59.616
Once you cease teaching
respect (indistinct)

00:52:00.350 --> 00:52:02.352
or the government,

00:52:03.753 --> 00:52:07.757
once cynicism comes in, the
whole thing falls apart.

00:52:07.757 --> 00:52:09.259
And so I just,

00:52:12.462 --> 00:52:15.599
I feel hopeful, but
I think that it's,

00:52:15.599 --> 00:52:17.134
we're in a real
battle right now.

00:52:17.134 --> 00:52:19.669
There's no question about
it that every part of the,

00:52:19.669 --> 00:52:21.171
what I really meant to say

00:52:21.171 --> 00:52:24.374
was that the culture is the
thing that holds it together.

00:52:24.374 --> 00:52:26.243 align:start size:84% position:16%
You can vote for all
the right people,

00:52:26.243 --> 00:52:30.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
but if the culture itself,
if what you see on TV,

00:52:30.413 --> 00:52:33.717
if what is out there in the
culture and in the schools

00:52:33.717 --> 00:52:35.619
doesn't reinforce this idea,

00:52:35.619 --> 00:52:39.356
somebody I forget who called
it the habits of the heart.

00:52:39.356 --> 00:52:41.324
If we're not taught
to love our country,

00:52:41.324 --> 00:52:43.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a part in my book,
"If You Can Keep It."

00:52:43.160 --> 00:52:46.663
I remember in fifth grade, an
old teacher, her last year,

00:52:46.663 --> 00:52:48.765
let us outside on June 14th,

00:52:48.765 --> 00:52:50.333 align:start size:84% position:16%
was one of the last
days of school,

00:52:50.333 --> 00:52:51.768
to celebrate flag day.

00:52:51.768 --> 00:52:56.206 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it was this sacred
moment and she never said it.

00:52:57.374 --> 00:52:58.708
But she was teaching
us to love our country,

00:52:58.708 --> 00:53:02.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
to respect the flag
in the most sweet way.

00:53:02.579 --> 00:53:05.549
We've really ceased
doing that mostly.

00:53:05.549 --> 00:53:08.285 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think when you
see stewing that,

00:53:08.285 --> 00:53:11.755 align:start position:0%
politics will fail you,
culture is upstream of politics

00:53:11.755 --> 00:53:16.760 align:start position:0% line:0%
and conservatives and Christians
have notoriously abdicated

00:53:18.695 --> 00:53:20.964 line:0%
the world of culture

00:53:21.965 --> 00:53:23.200
as important as politics is.

00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:24.768
And you know it is,
and I know it is,

00:53:24.768 --> 00:53:26.036
we can't advocate culture,

00:53:26.036 --> 00:53:27.637 align:start size:88% position:13%
which is why I do
silly things like write

00:53:27.637 --> 00:53:29.306
"Donald the Caveman" books,

00:53:29.306 --> 00:53:32.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
and have a talk show where
I talked to novelists,

00:53:32.776 --> 00:53:34.277
and so on and so forth.

00:53:34.277 --> 00:53:39.182 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause I actually think that
is the part of the battle

00:53:40.317 --> 00:53:41.618 align:start size:84% position:16%
where we have failed
most miserably.

00:53:43.353 --> 00:53:46.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Metaxas, I will keep
fighting alongside of you.

00:53:46.456 --> 00:53:48.258
What do you think of that?

00:53:48.258 --> 00:53:50.527 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I'm so happy to
finally get to know you

00:53:50.527 --> 00:53:52.696
and it really,

00:53:54.130 --> 00:53:55.599
you're an encouragement
to me and to many people.

00:53:55.599 --> 00:53:57.133
So thank you for what you do

00:53:57.133 --> 00:53:59.869
and thanks for giving me an
opportunity to rant and rave.

00:53:59.869 --> 00:54:03.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just needed to get
those things off my chest.

00:54:03.006 --> 00:54:04.774
- Likewise, my pleasure.

00:54:04.774 --> 00:54:07.978
And we're gonna link
down to all the books.

00:54:07.978 --> 00:54:09.212
Wait, what's your Twitter?

00:54:09.212 --> 00:54:10.413
I'm not remembering it
off the top of my head.

00:54:10.413 --> 00:54:11.581 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's jus Eric Metaxas-
- Eric Metaxas.

00:54:11.581 --> 00:54:12.983 align:start size:81% position:19%
- That's it?
It's just my name,

00:54:12.983 --> 00:54:15.986 align:start position:0%
Eric Metaxas, Facebook, Twitter,
Instagram, Eric Metaxas.

00:54:17.354 --> 00:54:18.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
And YouTube channel.
- (indistinct) my friend.

